Subject: [PATCH] apps/crypto/mbedtls: lower NuttX mbedtls header priority

Apply to: apps/   (patch -p1 -d <workspace>/apps)

ESP-IDF (esp-hal-3rdparty) and NuttX each ship their own fork of mbedtls,
and the two disagree on struct layouts and on which config symbols exist.
apps/crypto/mbedtls/Make.defs adds the NuttX copy with -I, which places it
ahead of the ESP-IDF include paths for every translation unit, including
esp-hal sources.

As a result, building esp-hal files such as bootloader_sha.c pulls in the
NuttX check_config.h while the ESP-IDF config macros are in effect,
producing 7 errors of the form:

  error: "MBEDTLS_ECJPAKE_C defined, but not all prerequisites"
  error: "MBEDTLS_KEY_EXCHANGE_ECDH_RSA_ENABLED defined, but not all prerequisites"
  ...

Switching to -isystem keeps the NuttX headers reachable but places them
after the ESP-IDF ones, so esp-hal sources resolve to their own copy.

This mirrors fix 1 of the upstream script packages/ai_agent/fix_esp32s3.sh,
which applies the same change for ESP32-S3.

Required when CONFIG_CRYPTO_MBEDTLS=y on Espressif targets (i.e. whenever
CONFIG_EXAMPLES_AI_AGENT_VELA is enabled).

Verified on ESP32-P4, openvela / NuttX 13.0.0, 2026-09-13.
diff --git a/crypto/mbedtls/Make.defs b/crypto/mbedtls/Make.defs
index 3cb722d52..72dc8e4f5 100644
--- a/crypto/mbedtls/Make.defs
+++ b/crypto/mbedtls/Make.defs
@@ -23,10 +23,10 @@ CONFIGURED_APPS += $(APPDIR)/crypto/mbedtls
 
 # Allows `<mbedtls/<>.h>` import.
 
-CFLAGS += ${INCDIR_PREFIX}$(APPDIR)/crypto/mbedtls/include
-CFLAGS += ${INCDIR_PREFIX}$(APPDIR)/crypto/mbedtls/mbedtls/include
+CFLAGS += -isystem $(APPDIR)/crypto/mbedtls/include
+CFLAGS += -isystem $(APPDIR)/crypto/mbedtls/mbedtls/include
 
-CXXFLAGS += ${INCDIR_PREFIX}$(APPDIR)/crypto/mbedtls/include
-CXXFLAGS += ${INCDIR_PREFIX}$(APPDIR)/crypto/mbedtls/mbedtls/include
+CXXFLAGS += -isystem $(APPDIR)/crypto/mbedtls/include
+CXXFLAGS += -isystem $(APPDIR)/crypto/mbedtls/mbedtls/include
 
 endif
